<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<jmeterTestPlan version="1.2" properties="5.0" jmeter="5.6.3">
  <hashTree>
    <TestPlan guiclass="TestPlanGui" testclass="TestPlan" testname="IASG Monitor Manual and Automatic Modes">
      <stringProp name="TestPlan.comments">Step 10 - Monitor, Manual, and Automatic modes.

This plan repeats the Step 9 three-IP coordinated route-scanning scenario, then lets IP 198.51.100.21 make a configurable follow-up request after the agent cycle. JMeter does not change the dashboard mode or approve an instruction; those are deliberate human/runtime actions.

Monitor: select Monitor; use FOLLOWUP_REQUESTS=1 and EXPECTED_FINAL_STATUS=404. A recommendation appears but no policy is written.

Manual: select Manual; use MANUAL_APPROVAL_WAIT_MS=60000. During that pause, approve an action in the dashboard. For an approved throttle use FOLLOWUP_REQUESTS=40 and EXPECTED_FINAL_STATUS=429. For an approved temporary block use FOLLOWUP_REQUESTS=1 and EXPECTED_FINAL_STATUS=403. For no approval use 1 and 404.

Automatic: select Automatic; enable policy throttling in Settings; use FOLLOWUP_REQUESTS=40 and EXPECTED_FINAL_STATUS=429. The coordinated medium-severity scan normally creates an automatic throttle. The first burst requests can be 404 while its token bucket has capacity; the final verification request should be 429.

Before every mode run: clear campaigns, delete any live policy for these IPs, then start with fresh evidence. The dashboard reset does not remove an existing Redis policy key.</stringProp>
      <elementProp name="TestPlan.user_defined_variables" elementType="Arguments" guiclass="ArgumentsPanel" testclass="Arguments" testname="User Defined Variables">
        <collectionProp name="Arguments.arguments">
          <elementProp name="HOST" elementType="Argument">
            <stringProp name="Argument.name">HOST</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.value">${__P(HOST,localhost)}</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
          <elementProp name="PORT" elementType="Argument">
            <stringProp name="Argument.name">PORT</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.value">${__P(PORT,8082)}</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
          <elementProp name="SETUP_REQUESTS" elementType="Argument">
            <stringProp name="Argument.name">SETUP_REQUESTS</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.value">${__P(SETUP_REQUESTS,8)}</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
          <elementProp name="REPEAT_REQUESTS" elementType="Argument">
            <stringProp name="Argument.name">REPEAT_REQUESTS</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.value">${__P(REPEAT_REQUESTS,6)}</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
          <elementProp name="DECISION_ENGINE_WAIT_MS" elementType="Argument">
            <stringProp name="Argument.name">DECISION_ENGINE_WAIT_MS</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.value">${__P(DECISION_ENGINE_WAIT_MS,45000)}</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
          <elementProp name="MANUAL_APPROVAL_WAIT_MS" elementType="Argument">
            <stringProp name="Argument.name">MANUAL_APPROVAL_WAIT_MS</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.value">${__P(MANUAL_APPROVAL_WAIT_MS, 60000)}</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
          <elementProp name="FOLLOWUP_REQUESTS" elementType="Argument">
            <stringProp name="Argument.name">FOLLOWUP_REQUESTS</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.value">${__P(FOLLOWUP_REQUESTS,40)}</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
          <elementProp name="EXPECTED_FINAL_STATUS" elementType="Argument">
            <stringProp name="Argument.name">EXPECTED_FINAL_STATUS</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.value">${__P(EXPECTED_FINAL_STATUS,429)}</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
        </collectionProp>
      </elementProp>
    </TestPlan>
